<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN FD_Diagnostic CAN 0614 - 29 Bit</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>J1962 connector pins definition - Typically used for Powertrain CAN ECUs.

ECUs without a direct connection to the J1962 connector shall also support the 'ECU Specific CAN' interface.

Interface must be updated to match vehicle architecture.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>CAN_FD_Diagnostic_CAN_0614_29_Bit</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not supported</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>supported</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_00000271826BDBF0' oid='B41BFDD6A528490094ED3BCDD5ACD88E' temploid='BDC66CA14F0341c5B3311D4669D9E701' attrcatref='_0000027182560B30' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN FD_ECU Specific CAN - 29 Bit</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Used for ECUs without a direct connection to the J1962 connector. Bus name should be changed to match vehicle architecture definition. The appropriate  J1962 CAN bus shall also be defined in parallel.

Interface must be updated to match vehicle architecture.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>CAN_FD_ECU_Specific_CAN_29_Bit</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not supported</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>supported</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
