<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Bus Type</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Bus Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Type of transport media</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Type of transport media</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.BusType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Ethernet</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Ethernet</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182990880' oid='4247759ABDAA4141842059D19B276875' temploid='83FF89EF606B4727B8F6FA2D81471829' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='1' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>LogicalGatewayAddress</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>LogicalGatewayAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The logical address of the DoIP gateway. When addressing nodes behind a DoIP gateway, this address has to be used to reach the target addressed in CP_DoIPLogicalEcuAddress or CP_DoIPLogicalFunctionalAddress. For a DoIP node, the values for CP_DoIPLogicalGatewayAddress and CP_DoIPLogicalEcuAddress are identical.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>The logical address of the DoIP gateway. When addressing nodes behind a DoIP gateway, this address has to be used to reach the target addressed in CP_DoIPLogicalEcuAddress or CP_DoIPLogicalFunctionalAddress. For a DoIP node, the values for CP_DoIPLogicalGatewayAddress and CP_DoIPLogicalEcuAddress are identical.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_DoIPLogicalGatewayAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182991480' oid='B8C8329316EC46d09AC63426A02295F1' temploid='7B065A051C10476a9FA22FAFA62ECD7C' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='1' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>LogicalEcuAddress</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>LogicalEcuAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The target address of the ECU to communicate with. This is the logical address as defined by the OEM.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>The target address of the ECU to communicate with. This is the logical address as defined by the OEM.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_DoIPLogicalEcuAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182991880' oid='0E78C39970FE4e8eAE7AEA288C135370' temploid='454CC265E32345a69E769B213BC8BD5A' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='3584' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>LogicalTesterAddress</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>LogicalTesterAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The source address of the test equipment. This is the logical address as defined by the OEM.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>The source address of the test equipment. This is the logical address as defined by the OEM.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_DoIPLogicalTesterAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182990A80' oid='386FD6406C4346e6BF79B1FF67550887' temploid='A5668FEFFFBB4ea2BCBD3850AF64EF4D' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='58368' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>LogicalFunctionalAddress</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>LogicalFunctionalAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Logical address for functional addressed communication.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Logical address for functional addressed communication.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_DoIPLogicalFunctionalAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182992C80' oid='B5EB7392B9DB456c83071C69809B1374' temploid='38ADC479B16F4a2998557AB2C969DF39' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>LogicalEcuSecondaryResponseAddress</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>LogicalEcuSecondaryResponseAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Secondary  logical  ECU  address  delivered with ECU responses corresponding to CAN UUDT addressed responses. The special value of 0 is used to indicate that UUDT responses are not used.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Secondary  logical  ECU  address  delivered with ECU responses corresponding to CAN UUDT addressed responses. The special value of 0 is used to indicate that UUDT responses are not used.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_DoIPSecondaryLogicalEcuResponseAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182990480' oid='A94B87BA961E4874BC9925D97A7EDDEC' temploid='75E987A38FDA44f0B9F60B409EF02B81' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='1000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P6Client</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>P6Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a request message indicated via T_Data.con) for the complete reception of the corresponding response message (indicated via T_Data.ind). If the transport/network layer doesn't support the  T_DataSOM.ind interface (e.g. ISO13400 DoIP), this ComParam shall be used instead of P2Client.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Timeout for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a request message indicated via T_Data.con) for the complete reception of the corresponding response message (indicated via T_Data.ind). If the transport/network layer doesn't support the  T_DataSOM.ind interface (e.g. ISO13400 DoIP), this ComParam shall be used instead of P2Client.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_P6Max</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_000002718298F880' oid='DBBF969E443C44f9AEFAAE2F4911A840' temploid='22D88E23B1F148ecB5B39AE0F8AB8CEE' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='50' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Server</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>P2Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the reception of a request message. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.The tester will also require the P2Server timeout, since in UDS service "DiagnosticSessionControl"returns the P2Server and P2ExServer timeouts – the tester has to calculate the offset manually and has to add it to the returned P2Server and P2ExServer timeouts.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the reception of a request message. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.The tester will also require the P2Server timeout, since in UDS service "DiagnosticSessionControl"returns the P2Server and P2ExServer timeouts – the tester has to calculate the offset manually and has to add it to the returned P2Server and P2ExServer timeouts.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_P2Max_Ecu</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_000002718298F480' oid='CE4B3CB984E242b4BD534228C3A098A0' temploid='6323E80014704c13A16F67ECDEB30166' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='10000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P6ExClient</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>P6ExClient</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Enhanced timeout for the client to wait after the reception of a negative response message  with negative response code 0x78 (indicated via T_Data.ind) for the complete reception  of  the corresponding response messages (indicated via T_Data.ind). If  the transport/network  layer doesn't support the T_DataSOM.ind interface (e.g. ISO13400 DoIP), this ComParam shall be used instead of P2ExClient.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Enhanced timeout for the client to wait after the reception of a negative response message  with negative response code 0x78 (indicated via T_Data.ind) for the complete reception  of  the corresponding response messages (indicated via T_Data.ind). If  the transport/network  layer doesn't support the T_DataSOM.ind interface (e.g. ISO13400 DoIP), this ComParam shall be used instead of P2ExClient.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_P6Star</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182991080' oid='DA7987544CB04623B2317C6BBED9A276' temploid='284CEEBC7F5746858E0651293341760E' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='5000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2ExServer</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>P2ExServer</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the transmission of a negative response message with response code 78 hex (enhanced response timing). In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the transmission of a negative response message with response code 78 hex (enhanced response timing). In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_P2Star_Ecu</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182992680' oid='6C6CF07B8C55459a9A712A23716B9652' temploid='984BF1883798422dADC5E658873462C4' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='2000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Client</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>S3Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time between functionally addressed Tester Present request messages transmitted by the client to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active in multiple servers (functional communication) or maximum time between physically transmitted request messages to a single server (physical communication).</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Time between functionally addressed Tester Present request messages transmitted by the client to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active in multiple servers (functional communication) or maximum time between physically transmitted request messages to a single server (physical communication).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_TesterPresentTime</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182991C80' oid='A15A3AF09AB44355BD955AB347AD22B4' temploid='F8B9C85AA70A4c50BC878F673FA8217E' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='5000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Server</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>S3Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for the server to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active while not receiving any diagnostic request message.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Time for the server to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active while not receiving any diagnostic request message.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_TesterPresentTime_Ecu</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182990280' oid='9216D251D29A460dB3749D4D73EDC6A1' temploid='4C45250EBBA84a6e9CDBB8081B0ED265' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='50' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientPhys</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>P3ClientPhys</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a physically addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) with no response required before it can transmit the next physically addressed request message.  Minimum value = P2Server.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a physically addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) with no response required before it can transmit the next physically addressed request message.  Minimum value = P2Server.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_P3Phys</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182991E80' oid='F0D05FA4408B425a991C163822BDE51C' temploid='E5F165E0AA764244B07ADD21B67EFF02' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='50' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientFunc</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>P3ClientFunc</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a functionally addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) before it can transmit the next functionally addressed request message in case no response is required or the requested data is only supported by a subset of the functionally addressed servers.  Minimum value = P2Server.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a functionally addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) before it can transmit the next functionally addressed request message in case no response is required or the requested data is only supported by a subset of the functionally addressed servers.  Minimum value = P2Server.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_P3Func</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182990C80' oid='6B298FD5D4EC4d6d864E1653322A91C3' temploid='C4389DED4A5D46258578BF936D8CFF42' attrcatref='_0000027182560A70' usage='admin' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TransmissionTime</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>TransmissionTime</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>If the timeout values are used which have been received by the ECU via session control response(0x50), the Network transmission time has to be added to the timeout values. P6 = received P2 + NetworkTransmissionTime(contains delay for both transmission directions).</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>If the timeout values are used which have been received by the ECU via session control response(0x50), the Network transmission time has to be added to the timeout values. P6 = received P2 + NetworkTransmissionTime(contains delay for both transmission directions).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_NetworkTransmissionTime</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_00000271829B8D80' oid='26AD542183814d9aB3D5144DA8FFDA7D' temploid='E9BD9CA49F134ec1B566FBEDE2762CFC' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='2' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>RC78Handling</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>RC78Handling</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Handling of 0x7F XX 0x78 ResponseTimeout and 0x78 Repetitions. The receive timeout value will be CP_P6Star. This timer will be reset on each consecutive reception of the 0x7F 0x78 response.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Handling of 0x7F XX 0x78 ResponseTimeout and 0x78 Repetitions. The receive timeout value will be CP_P6Star. This timer will be reset on each consecutive reception of the 0x7F 0x78 response.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_RC78Handling</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Disabled</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Disabled</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Continue until RC78 timeout</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Continue until RC78 timeout</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='2'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Continue unlimited</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Continue unlimited</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000027182992480' oid='5C32D63F103E416bA991AA9EB8B8FC43' temploid='C3EBBC319DC24ff9BB958BDB41D9F20F' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='25000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>RC78CompletionTimeout</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>RC78CompletionTimeout</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time period the tester accepts repeated negative responses with response code 0x78 and waits for a positive response further on.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Time period the tester accepts repeated negative responses with response code 0x78 and waits for a positive response further on.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_RC78CompletionTimeout</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_00000271829B7C10' oid='571B3B6E187F48968318FF6BEBB5A551' temploid='762B9E3494234e379182753763889A50' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>RC21Handling</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>RC21Handling</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Repetition mode in case of response code 0x7F XX 0x21.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Repetition mode in case of response code 0x7F XX 0x21.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_RC21Handling</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Disabled</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Disabled</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Continue until RC21 timeout</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Continue until RC21 timeout</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='2'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Continue unlimited</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Continue unlimited</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_000002718298F080' oid='57BAE110F2CF4fdeBD6DF276C80EDDBE' temploid='ED4293D12BA743deB6046A2FA4929144' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='200' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>RC21RequestTime</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>RC21RequestTime</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time between negative response with response code 0x21 and the retransmission of the same request.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Time between negative response with response code 0x21 and the retransmission of the same request.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_RC21RequestTime</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_000002718298F280' oid='269C1E39291B41568D17F594210F6590' temploid='889D9308CF7F44968014FE5A34919A71' attrcatref='_00000271825623F0' usage='admin' v='1300' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>RC21CompletionTimeout</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>RC21CompletionTimeout</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time period the tester accepts repeated negative responses with response code 0x21 and repeats the same request. Timer is started after reception of first negative response.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Time period the tester accepts repeated negative responses with response code 0x21 and repeats the same request. Timer is started after reception of first negative response.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Diagnostic_DoIP_ISO13400_2012.CP_RC21CompletionTimeout</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
