<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(ASR DEM) Defines the Step size for decrementation (PREPASSED). Range 0 - 127</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_STEP_SIZE_PREPASSED</QUAL>
</UNSRECORDITEMTMPL>
<ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271859927B0' oid='083A4331A2894fb59AC7504842734EC1' temploid='62E799B9AA974fab92E268C8C8A35D0D' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Use Jump-Up (Prefailed)</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(ASR DEM) Switch for the activation of Jump-UP:
Jump to Zero upon a change of the reported result (i.e. when after a sequence of 'prepassed' the result changes to 'prefailed')</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_JUMP_UP_PREFAILED</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>No</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Yes</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL>
<ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL id='_0000027185991AA0' oid='D73ED1DD4EF14ef1B672C8E36BF3F597' temploid='5EC926ED11B2472f9736828AE5B285B0' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Use Jump-Down (Prepassed)</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(ASR DEM) Switch for the activation of Jump-Down – only in combination with Jump-UP activation:
Jump to Zero upon a change of the reported result (i.e. when after a sequence of 'prefailed' the result changes to 'prepassed')</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_JUMP_DOWN_PREPASSED</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>No</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Yes</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL>
<ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL id='_0000027185991F60' oid='634F7C89F73B4081A9229C5A80C9E5CC' temploid='210C30DD4208429fB1D4B63EC08D879E' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Set WarningIndicatorBit at fault</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(ASR DEM) Yes -  the warningIndicatorRequested bit (bit 7) will be set at the same time as the confirmedDTC bit (bit 3) is set.
No - the warningIndicatorRequested bit (bit 7) is 0 at all times.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_WARNING_INDICATOR_FLAG</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>supported</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not supported</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL>
<UNSRECORDITEMTMPL id='_000002718267B830' oid='3C8F94DA768A4fe1A4E3E4105B96EF1D' temploid='9337448C222E485999CA41EE266FAAE0' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' df='hex' v='255'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Unit</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(ASR DEM) Can be used to identify the corresponding basic vehicle / system function which monitors this DTC.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_FUNCTIONAL_UNIT_VALUE</QUAL>
</UNSRECORDITEMTMPL>
<UNSRECORDITEMTMPL id='_000002718267D5F0' oid='089B3B5C944744c5B185FD599038EF92' temploid='339AFA87EF5A4f958A473043885048E4' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt' df='dec' v='0'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DTC Debounce Failed Timeout Value</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(ASR DEM) This parameter defines the time [ms] for event failed qualification of the DTC specific time based debouncing.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_TIMEOUT_VALUE_PREFAILED</QUAL>
</UNSRECORDITEMTMPL>
<UNSRECORDITEMTMPL id='_000002718267DB40' oid='B334E8F7E94B4052B47AFC6658C23819' temploid='FB29614080F6487099754C380EAC45DA' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt' df='dec' v='0'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DTC Debounce Passed Timeout Value</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(ASR DEM) This parameter defines the time [ms] for event passed qualification of the DTC specific time based debouncing.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_TIMEOUT_VALUE_PREPASSED</QUAL>
</UNSRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271D4621F30' oid='4514F805D41A4f18B1BA3943090EEA52' temploid='DB3096756BB14e89B62AC44C78C700C3' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Stored DTC Self Healing Criteria</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Criteria - in addition to SID $14 - used to erase a DTC from the fault memory.   Include Configuration dependencies.  (e.g. “100 consecutive key cycles of 'STORED' DTC”).</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Stored_DTC_Self_Healing_Criteria</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B0180' oid='D4A2F98C93134032976E3C424D654576' temploid='3C9BF5732E474b1492A408B2A8B483A3' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Customer Perception Symptom</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Description of how the fault affects the system and how it may be perceived by the customer (e.g. “headlamps commanded on when the bus network is not communicating”) </TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Customer_Perception_Symptom</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B0A80' oid='B3A0195DAD25431fA48DFE462FD9811C' temploid='0913FFB478F84a2e94C95CCF11EBD345' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Possible Causes</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Indicates the most probable recognizable cause of the failure in the ECU in the order from most probable to least probable. At a minimum it is required to provide the most probable reason, for example:
1.        Feature not learned
2.        Relay missing</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Possible_Causes</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B0380' oid='ACC6066FEB264e59B0632CC39A07DCF8' temploid='E647C151EC0342baB61A28A00BFDDD49' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Repair Action</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Description of action required for possible fault correction or for further fault analysis. Action instructions only relate to faults that can be rectified by the service department or in production (i.e. to the smallest replaceable unit). </TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Repair_Action</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B1780' oid='62629DA0D5A04769AFCEE7781782ADA7' temploid='9E7C00504B2B4112B105F21B57DB333B' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Level-Specific Enable Conditions</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) System operating conditions that must be satisfied prior to checking for 'Mature Criteria'.  Include Configuration dependencies.
Its recommend to use enable conditions number (EC x) as shown in table 17 of CS-11736.  Example of LoC DTC enable condtions:
EC 1- DTC Setting
EC 2 - Ignition Status
EC 4 - System Voltage
EC 6 - Network Configuration Status
EC 7 - Bus Physical Status
EC 9 - De-bounce Timer</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Level_Specific_Enable_Conditions</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B2380' oid='03521473C8E64d689278243281698D9A' temploid='79EE3126812844d2B81509A2CE68D7DA' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mature Threshold</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Physical conditions that must be met for the DTC to transition to 'ACTIVE' or 'PENDING' (e.g. “&#60; 0.8 volts”).   Indicates the conditions that must be met for the DTC to be set (e.g. “Sensor value &#60; 0.8 volts”, “Sensor value &#62; 4.5 volts”). "Implausible" conditions must be explained.   For Loss of Comm and Implausible DTCs list actual signal and/or message name.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mature_Threshold</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B2680' oid='D72B111C95244db68EB2FB6E8256C0E3' temploid='811C2793DDFC489d9BC8432B83045DE1' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Monitor Type</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Defines the various types of DTC monitoring strategies that are defined for each DTC:

•Continuous – ECU checks for a failure at a predefined rate (e.g.: every 10 ms the circuit is checked for a short to ground condition). ECU checks for this condition pre predefined rate (e.g.: every 10 ms the circuit is checked for a short to ground condition). ECU checks for this condition pre and post fault setting. This allows for the ECU to de-mature an active fault condition in the same operation cycle.

• Latching - ECU checks for a failure at a predefined rate (e.g.: every 10 ms the circuit is checked for a short to ground condition) up to the point of setting an active failure. Once an active failure is set for the operation cycle, the ECU disables fault checking until the next operation cycle (e.g. until ignition has been switched off and on again). This monitoring type should only be used if required for safety reasons or to protect the ECU from being damaged.

• On-Demand - ECU checks for a failure when a device is commanded in a specific state (e.g.: ECU checks for a short to ground when the device is commanded on). Typically used on output devices or failures which are tested once during startup / initialization.</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Monitor_Type</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B0B80' oid='901BC9A3905941b393D119024BFDF37E' temploid='5EF280A3A01E4459980ED8D5AA1C712F' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>De-Mature Criteria</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Physical conditions that must be met for the DTC to transition to 'STORED' (e.g. “&#62; 0.8 volts”)</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>De_Mature_Criteria</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B2D80' oid='9B47EABCE01C4ca1AECCB1F20B717F80' temploid='5E201712C01544a1AC9CBA8260CACA57' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Occurrence / Fault</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) DTC is identified as a fault or an occurrence. 
There is no added benefits to the technician to have the DTC set to "Occurrence," there is a problem with system and it needs to be addressed.  If you are concerned with the ECU being blamed for vehicle problem you must review the diagnostic service manuals to ensure that you agree with the diagnostic procedure.

System over-/under-voltage failures as well as local over-/under-voltage failures shall be classified as occurrences rather than a fault.

DTC Environmental Data inludes "Occurrence Flag" where ECU inditifes 1 bit 0 = Fault and 1 = Occurrence</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Occurrence_Fault</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000271855B2F80' oid='94918A50EAEB4ba483EDB517272F318F' temploid='23522A06C1BA49faBB4015EAAD91F7F5' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Limp In Action (Recovery)</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(FCA Attribute) Corrective or failsafe action taken by the ECU when DTC is 'ACTIVE' (e.g. “default the headlamps on”)</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Limp_In_Action_Recovery</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
</RECORDTMPL>
