<TUV xml:lang='it'>Scan Tool Vehicle information</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Scan_Tool_Vehicle_information</QUAL>
<DIAGINST id='_0000027187DA5BF0' oid='291733309C6640dcA9A405564FDEE798' temploid='38EC37873A7F49918E9FD69525E63CD5' tmplref='_00000271860B9330' act='0' xaud='32' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>WWH-OBD GTR Number</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'>MessageCount CALID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0' struct='1'><PARA><FC>ECU response at request PID $03 of service $09 is follow descrive:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Tx 2 (bytes)	F1-&#62;33 : 09 03 </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Rx 4 (bytes)	10-&#62;F1 : 49 03 01 01 </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>That means:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Number Of Data Items = 01</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Message Count CALID = 01</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>Number Of Data Items:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This parameter defines the number of data items included in the response message which are identified and belong to the InfoType reported;</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>In ECU Marelli 6F3, a request message with the InfoType $03 for MessageCountCALID, the response is positive with $01 value because the message is included into anly one message</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>Message Count CALID:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Number of messages to report calibration identifications</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Support for ISO 15765-4 is not required for the ECU and the external test equipment. In For ECU Marelli 6F3 the response is positive con message Count CALID = $01, that means the CALID is included in only one message</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>WWH_OBD_GTR_Number</QUAL>
<SERVICE id='_000002718819EEF0' oid='7747C5C069524e87AC9E1CED4C3E0F04' temploid='4995BAC95DDB4722A43761A67253EB02' tmplref='_00000271860F8430' func='1' phys='0' respOnPhys='0' respOnFunc='1' xaud='32' req='0'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Vehicle Info</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Vehicle Info</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Vehicle_Info</QUAL>
<SHORTCUTNAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>WWH-OBD GTR Number Vehicle Info</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</SHORTCUTNAME>
<SHORTCUTQUAL>WWH_OBD_GTR_Number_Vehicle_Info</SHORTCUTQUAL>
</SERVICE>
<STATICVALUE oid='37D22E41A9824e6098337E31E70B8FCB' temploid='0EB4A428BB284e07A70FBCEF058A041B' shstaticref='_0000027186177F50' v='17'/>
<SIMPLECOMPCONT oid='FE6A5B65CC934bfc90C90E3FBAF11535' temploid='09B80151D4054ef0989CBB1F64FEE972' shproxyref='_00000271860B9220'>
<DATAOBJ oid='66B4BF3273AD43639738C22FA3F13F16' temploid='89C19745BAA445a88785EB70BEF8F884' spec='no' v='1' dtref='_0000027182C4A5B0'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>NumberOfDataItems</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>NumberOfDataItems</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>This parameter defines the number of data items included in the response message which are identified and
belong to the InfoType reported. For example, a request message with the InfoType for CVN (Calibration
Verification Number) may cause the ECU to send a response message, that contains multiple CVNs. The amount
of CVNs is included in the “Number of data items” parameter</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Questo parametro definisce il numero di data items inclusi nel messaggio di risposta che sono identificati e 
appartengono all'InfoType riportato. Per esempio, un messaggio di richiesta con InfoType per CVN (Calibration
Verification Number) può comportare che la ECU invii un messaggio di risposta che contiene multipli CVN. La quantità 
di CVN è inclusa nel parametro "Numero di data items".</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>NumberOfDataItems</QUAL>
</DATAOBJ>
<DATAOBJ oid='F4FDC4E26D9C46e1B2164B1A09AAEC17' temploid='D2007685E9364d14937D03E7D1EE3CE9' spec='no' dtref='_00000271847015D0'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>WWH-OBD GTR Number</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'>MessageCount CALID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'></TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'>number of message for calibration value define
(CALID)</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>WWH_OBD_GTR_Number</QUAL>
</DATAOBJ>
</SIMPLECOMPCONT>
