<DIAGINST id='_000002718829E370' oid='999D0ED02A65462e868D95188DA97C96' temploid='DF43DF5565B841c98C4B1562796347B6' tmplref='_00000271860B9330' act='0' xaud='32' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>MessageCount VIN</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>MessageCount VIN</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'></TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0' struct='1'><PARA><FC>ECU response at request PID $01 of service $09 is follow descrive:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Tx 2 (bytes)	F1-&#62;33 : 09 01 </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Rx 4 (bytes)	10-&#62;F1 : 49 01 01 01 </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>That means:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Number Of Data Items = 01</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC>Message Count VIN = 01</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>Number Of Data Items:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This parameter defines the number of data items included in the response message which are identified and belong to the InfoType reported;</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>In ECU Marelli 6F3, a request message with the InfoType $01 for MessageCount VIN, the response is positive with $01 value because the message is included into anly one message</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>Message Count VIN:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Number of messages to report Vehicle Identification Number (VIN)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Support for ISO 15765-4 is not required for the ECU and the external test equipment.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>For ECU Marelli 6F3 the response is positive con message Count VIN = $01, that means the VIN is included in only one message</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>MessageCount_VIN</QUAL>
